<title>UK: Sonatrach raises Oct gas oil premium to $2.50.</title>
<headline>Sonatrach raises Oct gas oil premium to $2.50.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-09-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>State Algerian oil company Sonatrach has raised prices for October delivery gas oil by $1.50 a tonne, contract traders said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>They said Sonatrach had announced a premium of $2.50 over the formula for low sulphur gas oil cargoes to be delivered in October, against the $1 premium it asked in September.</p>
<p>Sonatrach is expected to deliver eight to nine contract cargoes in October.</p>
<p>-- Melanie Goodfellow, London Newsroom +44 171 542 7714</p>
